ed_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:73ae5b7e29a3a29ca61f2e2b7281184aabe2d05591c99fa4cb084ff5a2fd9566","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T03:09:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T03:09:36Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1210-v0.12.10/m12stage10-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1210-v0.12.10","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1210-v0.12.10","body":"# Engacer OS M12.10 / 0.12.10 - Grouped taskbar\n\nM12-STAGE10-VM-v1 native qualification passes. Public release and complete website verification are pending before M12.11.\n\nBuild: `3cc55b89594d7e8d0902d44324beb97c`.\nISO SHA256: `ec0a755a44b994460a95e4205136848286cd92ed328f8b036e6a28cb23d62b2f`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `2780c528681ad511b5a0fca6b8e33ab78618236be9bbc21735b21506d314b404`.\n\n## What changes\n\nOne app button now combines its pin and open windows, using the shared original\nicon and canonical app identity. Single-window buttons minimize/restore; several\nwindows open a numbered folder/document chooser. Counts, active indicators and\nminimized-only dots distinguish actual state. A hidden active app highlights\nMore apps. Overflow focuses/restores rather than minimizing the selected app.\n\nPins retain per-user order and alignment. Unpinned running apps stay reachable;\nfirst-appearance ordering prevents window focus/Z-order changes from moving\nbuttons. Overflow is bounded and paginated when thirteen hidden apps cannot fit\nthe twelve-item menu. New-window requests retain the eight-window limit.\n\nContext close keeps dirty-work review and file-dialog owner guards. Unpinning\nkeeps the app, data and windows. Software Manager refuses removal while an app\nis open; after closing it, removal prunes its pin/group and reinstall works.\n\n## How and why\n\nDerive the unique app union from existing pin/window identities, reusing the\nwindow manager, validated version-one preferences and generation tokens. Fixed\nshared chooser labels and a small nonpersistent order array avoid dangling label\npointers and moving buttons. There is no per-window preview framebuffer, extra\nprocess or idle animation. [Design decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/docs/architecture/taskbar-m1210.md),\n[taskbar guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/docs/handbook/taskbar-m1210.md) and\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/docs/handbook/install-m1210.md).\n\n## Verification\n\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/evidence/M12/10/acceptance-results.json) records\n590 compiled Git inputs; actual keyboard/mouse group launch, minimize/restore,\nwindow choice, dirty close, owner protection, pin ordering/removal, in-use refusal,\npackage removal/reinstall, eight-window overflow and ordinary installed starts.\nCompact light/dark, 150% and actual 3840x2160/200% cover real menus and review.\nThe compact maximum case uses eight pins plus eight distinct running apps and\nreaches the second overflow page. Host production union/order/layout checks\ncover 295907 assertions. The actual decoder passes 553 pages and 10808\nmalformed/fuzz cases with unchanged guard bytes. Separate matching VMware/BIOS\ninstallation, twelve cached/full movement comparisons and actual compressed\nboot repair pass for these exact bytes.\n\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/evidence/M12/10/resources.json) distinguish fixed state, peak\nand retained pages. Compiled fixed shell state is 552925 bytes, 840 above M12.9.\nShared font bytes stay unchanged; no raster/preview cache or new worker is\nintroduced. Configured guest RAM is not measured OS consumption.\n\n## Scope and retained limits\n\n- Grouping covers native catalogue identities and retains the eight-window quota.\n- Window switcher/snap refinements follow separately in M12.11.\n- M12.14 retains shared menu/footer/conflict and Start query/notice feedback,\n  plus background transfer/file-dialog arbitration. Finish/cancel transfers\n  before opening a picker until that integration gate is qualified.\n- M12.16 retains cursor isolation and small-mode versus explicit scale limits.\n- The earlier concurrent BIOS/AHCI observation and complete final controller/\n  original-app matrix remain M12.18; this stage does not establish stress reliability.\n- Physical/ARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal Windows compatibility remain unqualified.\n- Agent visual/scenario checks are not a human usability study. GitHub downloads\n  and complete public website proof close separately before M12.11.\n\n![Actual native grouped taskbar and window chooser](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/1fdebf6ff7604bd2503bf8acf2ddfd69ade73cc2/evidence/M12/10/feature.png)\n"}